        "subject": "LU-20879 osd-ldiskfs: match osd-zfs on a repeated destroy",
        "message": "LU-20879 osd-ldiskfs: match osd-zfs on a repeated destroy\n\nosd-ldiskfs osd_destroy() did not account for an object that has\nalready been destroyed.  Return -ENOENT when obj->oo_destroyed is\nset, as osd-zfs osd_destroy() already does, so that a repeated\ndestroy of the same object is handled consistently across backends.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=replay-single,recovery-small env=mdscount=2,mdtcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Idc76bed06af4020dfb779a73b773472ee13ebbe5\n"
